Please note we do not follow conventional wisdom for determining binary
source files.  We use file wildcard globing to determine source files.
Most people say that's a no-no, I don't agree.

To add source files to any of these libraries just add the files to the
corresponding library directory, from example put C files in quickdraw/
to add to the libquickdraw library (libquickdraw.so and libquickdraw.a).
You may want to touch any meson.build file after adding C files, if you
will re-run "meson compile" in the top build directory (or equivalent
such command).

If you wish to use the same C source file in two different libraries just
make a symlink, avoid adding redundant copies of files to the source of
this software project.

